    "Commitment/Consistency": {"Explanation": "Not present. There is no reference to prior behavior or choices that would encourage further action based on commitment or consistency."},
    "Liking": {"Explanation": "Not present. There is no personalization, flattery, or use of familiarity to build trust or rapport."},
    "Social proof": {"Explanation": "Not present. There is no mention of other people's participation or endorsements to support the offer. However, the forward to a friend option could be seen as a subtle social proof mechanism, but it is not prominently featured in the main content of the email."}
}

